WEBVTT

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.604
At five fifty-five,
the doors open in five minutes.

00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:06.270
The welcome desk has one guest list.

00:00:06.687 --> 00:00:08.440
The floor manager has another.

00:00:08.856 --> 00:00:10.020
Which one runs the room?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.412
Cuebook puts the people
producing your event on one plan.

00:00:13.836 --> 00:00:18.190
We bring it to corporate productions
and to approved nonprofit partnerships.

00:00:18.606 --> 00:00:21.954
Here's how the work moves from
the first brief to the last guest.

00:00:22.214 --> 00:00:23.349
Start with the brief.

00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:26.589
Set the venue, timing, and guest journey.

00:00:27.006 --> 00:00:28.802
Turn the plan into a run of show.

00:00:29.219 --> 00:00:30.397
Give each cue an owner,

00:00:30.785 --> 00:00:32.940
so everyone knows who makes the next move.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.556
The right vendor changes
what you can deliver.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.069
We compare fit, availability, and scope,

00:00:39.457 --> 00:00:41.282
then coordinate the approved team.

00:00:41.699 --> 00:00:44.716
We’ve worked on more than
two hundred and fifty small

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.805
and midsize events,
alongside our corporate work.

00:00:48.065 --> 00:00:49.516
When the doors open early,

00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:51.269
the lead updates the schedule.

00:00:51.693 --> 00:00:53.733
The welcome desk sees the change.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.975
The floor team knows when to move.

00:00:56.391 --> 00:00:59.409
Each person works from
the information their role needs.

00:00:59.669 --> 00:01:02.068
Guests confirm on a branded event page.

00:01:02.492 --> 00:01:05.509
At check-in, staff can
find the guest or their

00:01:05.524 --> 00:01:08.599
companion and validate
each arrival separately.

00:01:09.015 --> 00:01:11.573
Now both desks can work
from the same list.

00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:14.807
For foundations,
the approved setup can also

00:01:14.821 --> 00:01:19.505
support donations, volunteer sign-ups,
and sponsorship packages.

00:01:19.929 --> 00:01:22.429
Your organization controls its records.

00:01:22.846 --> 00:01:26.725
Sponsors see only the information
they've been authorized to receive.

00:01:26.985 --> 00:01:29.816
Vendor onboarding and contracts
are on the roadmap.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.702
A branded mobile app is
a separate, scoped decision.

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:36.562
We'll walk through those
requirements with you before

00:01:36.605 --> 00:01:38.013
either becomes a commitment.

00:01:38.273 --> 00:01:41.319
Platform setup and access
come at no additional

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:45.600
charge with full corporate production
or an approved nonprofit engagement.

00:01:46.024 --> 00:01:48.826
Your team can use Cuebook
again for future events.

00:01:49.243 --> 00:01:51.312
Tell VNV Support about yours.
